# Scratch, and only scratch.
#
# build/ is where every stage writes what the next stage reads: the derived
# plan, the staged pinned zones, the assembled door before it is copied out.
# None of it is a record and none of it is published — but it sits inside the
# published tree, so without this line one `git add -A` puts a build's private
# working state on the site. That nearly happened on 2026-08-24.
reader/build/
reader/site/
reader/deploy-root/

# count-gate-rule-v1 · a book is PUBLISHED when the count gate passed it.
#
# This site is served as a whole tree, so a committed zone file is a readable
# book whether or not any page links to it. Withholding an address and
# leaving the data is a door that says nothing is served while everything
# still is. So the safe state is the default: zone data is not published, and
# a book that passes the gate is added on purpose (git add -f), which is the
# one place publishing should ever be a decision somebody makes.
#
# The bins stay on disk — the builder reads them — they are simply not in the
# tree. check-bookword-count-v1 L4 holds the line from the other side.
reader/data/zones/*.bin
!reader/data/zones/fixture-*.bin
